  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ASHOKA | Hope Telemedicine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Every minute on average a woman dies worldwide from complications related to a lack of blood. Moreover, in developing countries, up to 65% of blood transfusions are administered to children under 5 years of age. (Sources: WHO). Our ambition with the HOPE project is to fight effectively against the lack of blood in health structures. In other words, no human life lost, no delayed surgery, no treatment of children with haemophilia or sickle cell disease, ...etc. The innovations introduced by the HOPE project will be the standards used in all African countries and even in the world to fight against blood shortages in blood structures.</narrative>
  </description>
